      "message": {
        "content": "{\n  \"chapter_proposals\": [\n    {\n      \"chapter_id\": \"CH04\",\n      \"title\": \"治疗干预：FMT、益生菌与饮食调节的可行性\",\n      \"purpose\": \"评估微生物群干预在临床实践中可靠增强 ICI 疗效的可行性，区分已验证的临床信号与探索性策略。\",\n      \"scope\": \"涵盖 FMT、活体生物药（LBP/益生菌）、饮食及代谢物干预的人类临床数据（主要为 I/II 期及观察性队列）。重点分析干预方案异质性（供体、菌株、剂量）、安全性（irAE 发生率）与 ICI 方案（单药 vs 双免疫）的交互作用。排除血液系统恶性肿瘤除非机制明确可转移至实体瘤。\",\n      \"excluded_source_handles\": [],\n      \"substantive_threads\": [\n        {\n          \"theme\": \"FMT 临床疗效的癌种与方案异质性\",\n          \"argument\": \"FMT 在 ICI 耐药或初治患者中的疗效并非均一，受肿瘤类型及 ICI 背景显著调节。FMT-LUMINate 试验显示 NSCLC 一线单药抗 PD-1 背景下 ORR 达 80%，黑色素瘤一线双免疫背景下 ORR 达 75%，但 GI 肿瘤（如 MITRIC 试验）在耐药背景下未显示显著获益（ORR 0%）。这种差异提示 FMT 可能更适用于特定免疫微环境（如'冷'转'热'潜力大）或特定 ICI 方案背景，而非通用增敏剂。\",\n          \"key_sources\": [\n            \"P0583\",\n            \"P0578\",\n            \"P0577\",\n            \"P0197\",\n            \"P0212\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"theme\": \"安全性信号与 ICI 方案的交互作用\",\n          \"argument\": \"FMT 的安全性高度依赖于联合的 ICI 方案。在双免疫检查点抑制剂（抗 PD-1+ 抗 CTLA-4）背景下，FMT 与显著升高的 3 级 + irAE 相关（65% 发生率，含心肌炎 15%），且起病更早（中位 40 天）；而在单药抗 PD-1 背景下（如 NSCLC 队列）未观察到 3 级 + AE。供体微生物特征（如 Prevotella 富集）可能与毒性风险相关，提示供体筛选需考虑 ICI 方案背景。\",\n          \"key_sources\": [\n            \"P0583\",\n            \"P0586\",\n            \"P0197\",\n            \"P0144\",\n            \"P0359\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"theme\": \"定义菌株与活体生物药（LBP）的早期证据\",\n          \"argument\": \"相比 FMT 的复杂性，定义菌株（如 CBM588, MRx0518）或共培养菌群（如 MaaT034, MET4）提供更标准化的干预路径。早期 I/II 期数据显示其安全性可控（如 MRx0518 在耐药实体瘤中 DCR 42%），并能诱导特定免疫变化（如 IgG 反应、T 细胞浸润），但临床疗效终点（ORR/OS）尚未在大规模试验中确证。商业混合益生菌可能因降低多样性而干扰 ICI 疗效，需区分'药物级 LBP'与'膳食补充剂'。\",\n          \"key_sources\": [\n            \"P0125\",\n            \"P0230\",\n            \"P0122\",\n            \"P0473\",\n            \"P0006\",\n            \"P0390\",\n            \"P0357\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"theme\": \"饮食与代谢物干预的观察性与干预性脱节\",\n          \"argument\": \"高纤维饮食、禁食及特定植物化合物（如多酚）在观察性队列中与 ICI 疗效正相关（如 PFS 改善），且机制上关联 SCFA 产生菌富集。然而，干预性数据有限且存在矛盾（如人工甜味剂可能削弱疗效）。代谢物补充（如丁酸盐）在临床前模型有效，但人体药代动力学及肿瘤微环境浓度数据缺失，限制了直接转化。\",\n          \"key_sources\": [\n            \"P0401\",\n            \"P0155\",\n            \"P0156\",\n            \"P0249\",\n            \"P0452\",\n            \"P0198\",\n            \"P0201\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"theme\": \"标准化实施障碍与转化路径\",\n          \"argument\": \"当前干预策略面临供体筛选标准不一、制备工艺差异、抗生素预处理策略冲突（如 SER-401 试验失败教训）及监管分类模糊等障碍。临床转化需从'经验性 FMT'转向'基于生物标志物的精准菌群工程'，并建立与 ICI 方案匹配的安全性监测体系。\",\n          \"key_sources\": [\n            \"P0178\",\n            \"P0387\",\n            \"P0573\",\n            \"P0516\",\n            \"P0534\",\n            \"P0503\"\n          ]\n        }\n      ],\n      \"supplement_requests\": [],\n      \"directed_reads\": [\n        \"P0583\",\n        \"P0578\",\n        \"P0586\",\n        \"P0125\",\n        \"P0230\"\n      ]\n    }\n  ],\n  \"screened_sources\": []\n}",
        "reasoning_content": "The user wants a chapter proposal for Chapter 4 (CH04) of a review on \"How does the gut microbiome modulate the efficacy of immune checkpoint inhibitors in solid tumours, and what mechanisms mediate that effect?\".\nThe chapter title is \"治疗干预：FMT、益生菌与饮食调节的可行性\" (Therapeutic Interventions: Feasibility of FMT, Probiotics, and Dietary Modulation).\nThe purpose is to evaluate the feasibility of microbiome interventions to reliably enhance ICI efficacy in clinical practice.\nThe scope adjustment emphasizes FMT safety data completeness (irAE rates, donor microbiome characteristics) but lack of standardized protocols; it needs to highlight intervention heterogeneity and toxicity signals interacting with ICI regimens.\nI need to use the provided `source_routing` and `chapter_tool_materials` to construct the proposal.\nI must follow the specific JSON structure for `chapter_proposals` and `screened_sources`.\nI need to ensure I don't just list sources but create a substantive argument structure (themes, cases, comparisons, synthesis).\nI need to respect the `interpretation_limits` for each source.\nI need to identify `supplement_requests` if there are genuine gaps that need targeted queries (though the prompt says \"limited supplementary search... does not equal lack of research\", I should only request if essential for the specific argument structure and not already covered by the routed pool).\nThe `shared_level1_outline` provides the context for the whole review.\nThe `source_routing` contains a large number of sources assigned to CH04. I need to select the most relevant ones for the specific themes of this chapter without listing all of them in the output (just use handles where necessary in the proposal text, but the JSON structure asks for `source_handles` in the chapter proposal? No, the instruction says \"Return chapter_proposals (each with chapter_id, title, purpose, scope, optional excluded_source_handles, substantive_threads, supplement_requests, directed_reads) and screened_sources with non-use reasons.\" It also says \"Do not silently drop a routed source: when an individual source is genuinely out of scope, name it in excluded_source_handles... otherwise retain it as writer-available material.\" However, the output format for `chapter_proposals` usually expects a list of sources or just the structure. Looking at the instruction: \"Return chapter_proposals... and screened_sources\". I should list the `source_handles` that are *planned* to be used or at least available for this chapter in the proposal section if possible, or rely on the `source_routing` which already assigned them. The instruction says \"Use the complete source_routing ledger... Do not discard routed sources merely because they were not deep-read\". So I should not exclude them unless they are truly out of scope. I will list the assigned handles in the chapter proposal's `source_handles` field if the schema allows, or just ensure they are not in `excluded_source_handles`. Wait, the instruction says \"Return chapter_proposals (each with chapter_id, title, purpose, scope, optional excluded_source_handles, substantive_threads, supplement_requests, directed_reads)\". It doesn't explicitly ask for a list of *included* handles in the chapter proposal object, but rather `excluded_source_handles`. However, to show I've planned the coverage, I should probably reference key handles in the `substantive_threads`.\nActually, looking at the `source_routing` provided in the input, many sources are assigned to CH04. I need to make sure I don't exclude them without reason.\nI need to draft the `substantive_threads` which describe the argument flow.\nI need to identify `supplement_requests` if there are specific gaps. The `chapter_tool_materials` provided specific data on FMT-LUMINate (NSCLC ORR 80%, Melanoma ORR 75%, toxicity in dual ICI). This is crucial.\nI need to check if there are gaps that require `supplement_requests`. The prompt says \"Every supplement_requests entry must include gap_id, gap_question, success_criteria, intended_use, and 1-2 targeted_queries\".\nGiven the rich source routing, I might not need many supplement requests unless there's a specific missing comparison (e.g., specific probiotic strains in specific cancer types not covered). The `shared_level1_outline` mentions \"limited supplementary search found no matching research...\". I should avoid creating supplement requests for things already covered by the routed pool. I will focus on structuring the existing material.\nHowever, the instruction says \"Every supplement_requests entry must include...\". If I don't have any, should I leave it empty? The instruction says \"Return chapter_proposals... and screened_sources\". It implies I should include `supplement_requests` if there are any. If none, I can leave the list empty. But I should check if there are genuine gaps. The `unresolved_limits` in the input mention \"Phase 3 RCT absence\" and \"Intratumoral metabolite quantification\". These are already noted in the shared outline. I don't need to request them again.\nI will focus on organizing the chapter argument.\n\nKey themes for CH04:\n1. FMT Clinical Evidence (Efficacy & Safety): FMT-LUMINate, MIMic, MITRIC. Contrast NSCLC vs Melanoma vs GI cancers. Highlight the dual-ICI toxicity signal.\n2. Probiotics & LBPs: Strain specificity (CBM588, MRx0518), commercial probiotics risks (Spencer et al.), mechanism vs clinical outcome.\n3. Dietary Modulation: Fiber, fasting, specific compounds (polyphenols). Observational vs Interventional.\n4. Standardization & Feasibility: Donor screening, preparation, regulatory hurdles, interaction with ICI regimen (mono vs dual).\n\nI need to make sure I don't overclaim efficacy (Phase 2 only).\nI need to integrate the safety signal (irAEs) prominently as per scope adjustment.\n\nLet's structure the `substantive_threads`.\nI will use the `source_routing` handles to support these threads.\nI will not exclude sources unless they are truly irrelevant (e.g. focused only on blood cancer without solid tumor mechanism transfer).\nI will check `screened_sources` for any sources from the pool that are truly unusable for this chapter (e.g. if a source is assigned to CH04 but actually only discusses blood cancer without solid tumor relevance). Looking at the routing, most are assigned to CH04 with specific usable material notes. I will keep them as available.\n\nI need to be careful with the `supplement_requests`. The instruction says \"Every supplement_requests entry must include...\". If I have none, I will return an empty list. Given the extensive routing, I likely don't need new searches for this chapter proposal, as the pool covers FMT, probiotics, diet. I will focus on synthesizing the existing routed material.\n\nLet's draft the JSON.\nChapter ID: CH04\nTitle: 治疗干预：FMT、益生菌与饮食调节的可行性\nPurpose: 评估微生物群干预在临床实践中可靠增强 ICI 疗效的可行性。\nScope: 聚焦 FMT、益生菌/活体生物药（LBP）、饮食干预的临床证据（主要为 I/II 期及观察性），强调方案异质性、安全性（irAE）与 ICI 方案的交互作用。排除血液肿瘤除非机制明确可转移。\n\nSubstantive Threads:\n1. FMT 临床转化现状：从概念验证到 II 期数据（FMT-LUMINate, MIMic, MITRIC）。对比不同癌种（NSCLC vs 黑色素瘤 vs GI）的 ORR 差异。\n2. 安全性与 ICI 方案交互：双免疫方案下的 irAE 风险（心肌炎、结肠炎）与供体菌群特征（Prevotella）的关联。单药 vs 联合的安全性差异。\n3. 益生菌与 LBP 的菌株特异性：CBM588, MRx0518 等定义菌株 vs 商业混合益生菌的矛盾证据（Spencer et al.）。\n4. 饮食与代谢物干预：高纤维、禁食、特定化合物（多酚）的观察性与干预性数据。机制与临床结局的脱节。\n5. 标准化与实施障碍：供体筛选、制备工艺、监管路径、与抗生素/合并用药的冲突。\n\nI will select key sources for each thread in the description.\nI will check for any sources that should be excluded. Most routed sources seem relevant. I will not exclude any unless I find a specific reason (e.g. P0004 is PDAC focused but has mechanism transferable, so keep. P0539 is blood cancer focused, might be excluded if no solid tumor mechanism, but routing says \"cross-system analogy\", so keep with caution).\nActually, I should check `screened_sources`. If I decide not to use a routed source for *this chapter* (even if assigned), I should list it in `excluded_source_handles` within the chapter proposal. But the instruction says \"Do not silently drop a routed source... otherwise retain it as writer-available material.\" So I only list excluded if genuinely out of scope. I will try to keep all assigned CH04 sources as available, maybe noting some are for background only.\nWait, `source_routing` shows many sources assigned to CH04. I will not list them all in `excluded_source_handles`. I will leave that empty or only include truly irrelevant ones.\nI will create `supplement_requests` only if I identify a specific gap not covered by the 590 candidate pool. Given the pool size and specific FMT data provided in `chapter_tool_materials`, I likely don't need new searches for the proposal. I will leave `supplement_requests` empty to avoid unnecessary queries, as the instruction says \"Evidence sufficient... do not force sources\".\n\nWait, I need to check the `chapter_tool_materials`. It provides specific data for FMT-LUMINate. This is high value. I must ensure this is central to the argument.\nI will structure the JSON carefully.\n\nOne more thing: \"Return JSON only.\"\nI need to make sure the JSON is valid.\nI will use the `source_handle` IDs from the routing.\nI will write the content in Chinese.\n\nLet's refine the `substantive_threads` to be more argumentative.\nThread 1: FMT Efficacy Heterogeneity. NSCLC (80% ORR) vs Melanoma (75% ORR) vs GI (lower/negative in MITRIC). Why? Baseline microbiome, ICI regimen.\nThread 2: Safety Signals. Dual ICI + FMT = High irAE (65% grade 3+). Mono ICI = Low irAE. Donor specific (Prevotella).\nThread 3: Defined Consortia vs FMT. MRx0518, MET4. Early safety/immunogenicity data.\nThread 4: Diet/Probiotics. Observational support (Fiber) vs Interventional ambiguity (Probiotics may hinder).\nThread 5: Implementation. Standardization gap.\n\nI will not add `supplement_requests` unless I find a critical missing piece. The `unresolved_limits` already cover Phase 3 absence. I don't need to query for that. I will leave `supplement_requests` as an empty list.\n\nI need to make sure I don't copy the `source_routing` content verbatim but use it to inform the proposal.\nI will list the `source_handles` that are *key* for the chapter in the `directed_reads` or just rely on the routing. The instruction says \"Return chapter_proposals... and screened_sources\". It doesn't explicitly require a list of *included* handles in the chapter proposal object, but `directed_reads` is a field. I will use `directed_reads` to highlight the most critical papers for deep reading (e.g. FMT-LUMINate, MIMic, MITRIC, key probiotic trials).\nActually, `directed_reads` is for \"any genuinely necessary tool needs\" or specific papers to focus on? The schema says `directed_reads`. I will use it to point to the key clinical trial reports that need careful extraction of safety/efficacy data.\n\nLet's finalize the structure.\n`chapter_proposals`: list of one object for CH04.\n`screened_sources`: list of sources that are excluded (if any). I will likely leave this empty as I plan to use the routed sources.\nWait, if I don't exclude any, `screened_sources` should be empty? Or should I list the ones I *am* using? The instruction says \"screened_sources with non-use reasons\". So only excluded ones.\nI will check if any assigned source is truly unusable. P0539 is blood cancer. Routing says \"cross-system analogy\". I can keep it but note the limitation. I won't exclude it unless it's purely blood cancer with no solid tumor mechanism. The routing says \"applicable to CH02/CH03/CH04\". I will keep it.\nI will focus on the `substantive_threads` to show the argument.\n\nOne detail: \"Do not discard routed sources merely because they were not deep-read\". So I should not exclude them in `excluded_source_handles` just because they are reviews vs primary. I will only exclude if the topic is completely off (e.g. purely blood cancer with no transferable mechanism). I think I can keep all assigned CH04 sources as available.\n\nLet's write the JSON.",
